2. Free Use

Subject to Sections 3-5, you may use, run, study, copy, modify and share
the Covered Material without charge. Personal use, private internal
company use and private classroom use remain free regardless of revenue.
Reading, citing findings and discussing aggregate results without
redistributing Covered Material do not require a commercial license.

3. Commercial Public Hosting and Distribution

A company with gross annual revenue strictly greater than US$1,000,000
must obtain a separate written commercial license from Licensor before
publicly hosting or distributing Covered Material. A company at exactly
US$1,000,000 does not cross this threshold. This requirement applies
whether the public offering is free or paid and regardless of revenue
earned specifically from this material.

Public hosting or distribution includes making Covered Material
available to the public through websites, repositories, downloads,
public services or products. Merely linking to the authorized official
release is not public hosting or distribution of Covered Material.
Private internal use is not public hosting or distribution.

For this threshold, gross annual revenue includes the company and its
controlled subsidiaries for the most recently completed fiscal year.
Non-USD revenue is converted using that year's average exchange rate
from a recognized public financial source.

Earlier license grants remain effective for the material they covered.
The exemptions and platform authorization in Section 4 also apply.

4. Educational Exemption and Official Distribution

Genuine schools, universities and nonprofit educational institutions
may publicly host or distribute Covered Material for teaching or
research without a commercial license, regardless of their revenue
or budget. Ordinary tuition and educational fees do not remove this
exemption. It does not cover commercial resale disguised as education
or a business distributing through an institution to avoid Section 3.

Licensor authorizes GitHub to host and distribute Licensor's official
upload under the permissions needed by GitHub's platform terms.
Existing platform distribution authorizations are not revoked.
This does not separately authorize an independent company above the
threshold to offer its own public mirror, service or distribution.

